<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander Obrenović</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1876">1876</a>–<a href="/years/1903">1903</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Alexander I of Serbia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander Obrenović was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> from 1889 to 1903. His authoritarian rule, suspension of the constitution and unpopular marriage to Draga Mašin alienated the army. In June 1903 officers murdered him and his queen in the palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obrenovic-dynasty">Obrenović dynasty</a> and bringing Peter I Karađorđević to the throne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-obrenovic.jpg" alt="Alexander Obrenović" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mijatovic, Cedomilj, 1842-1932 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AlejandroIDeSerbiaEn1900.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
